From 3072ad7c4d1304f34514741ea4a1f12c013989a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: giteaguy <73799093+irnutsmurt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:36:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] M10: display modes, a host frame limiter, the game held by
 its host, a port's own menu, bindings

- Vulkan window: PS3RECOMP_VK_DISPLAY_MODE windowed (resizable, PS3RECOMP_VK_WINDOW_RECT restored on a display
  that exists) / borderless / exclusive (the display's current mode, never another; refused: borderless);
  rsx_vulkan_backend_window_rect for the next session; PS3RECOMP_VK_WINDOW_HIDDEN for tests; VSync off falls
  back to MAILBOX without IMMEDIATE; the frame's aspect kept (black bars); a minimized window skips its presents
  and makes its swapchain again when back; live display-mode and VSync changes on the window's thread
  (rsx_vulkan_backend_request_display).
- include/ps3emu/guest_pause.h: the game held (every guest clock -- the timebase, sys_time_get_system_time,
  sys_time_get_current_time -- stands still; the render thread waits at its flip request); a host frame limiter
  at the flip request (a high-resolution waitable timer, then a yield); a clock warp (a time added to every
  guest clock, never decreasing).
- A port's own menu (osd.h g_ps3_osd_menu): its picture copied over the frame in each present, the last frame
  read back once for its background; g_ps3_host_close_request: the window's close and Escape asked first; the
  save screen's drawing public (ps3_ui_*).
- cellPad: cellPad_host_buttons / cellPad_host_keys (the pads, keys and mouse as they are, for a port's menu); a
  chord guard (a shortcut's buttons alone reach the game, the whole chord never); the player's bindings (each of
  the game's buttons from a pad button of their choice, applied to what the game is given; the keyboard's keys
  changeable, L3 and R3 on 3 and 4 by default).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
